WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.990
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.421
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.721 --> 00:00:13.986
Unit fourteen: Health & Body. Today you will give advice about staying healthy.

4
00:00:14.286 --> 00:00:16.880
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:21.205
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.330
Immune system.

7
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:27.767
Immune system means the part of your body that fights illness.

8
00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:30.302
Fruit helps your immune system.

9
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:33.929
Your turn. Say: Immune system.

10
00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.128
Immune system.

11
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:39.815
Symptom.

12
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:42.863
Symptom means a sign that you are ill.

13
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.868
A sore throat is a symptom of a cold.

14
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:48.753
Your turn. Say: Symptom.

15
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.555
Symptom.

16
00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:54.202
Recover.

17
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:57.472
Recover means to become healthy again.

18
00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.338
I recovered after two days in bed.

19
00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.463
Your turn. Say: Recover.

20
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.185
Recover.

21
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:08.812
Checkup.

22
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:12.896
Checkup means a visit to the doctor to see if you are healthy.

23
00:01:13.483 --> 00:01:15.367
I have a dental checkup tomorrow.

24
00:01:15.983 --> 00:01:18.206
Your turn. Say: Checkup.

25
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:21.882
Checkup.

26
00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:23.548
Posture.

27
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.956
Posture means the way you sit or stand.

28
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.782
Good posture protects your back.

29
00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:32.757
Your turn. Say: Posture.

30
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.485
Posture.

31
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:38.309
Stamina.

32
00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:42.442
Stamina means the energy to keep going for a long time.

33
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.748
Running builds stamina.

34
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.677
Your turn. Say: Stamina.

35
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:51.383
Stamina.

36
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.221
Hydrated.

37
00:01:54.217 --> 00:01:56.750
Hydrated means having enough water in your body.

38
00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.129
Stay hydrated in hot weather.

39
00:01:59.717 --> 00:02:02.276
Your turn. Say: Hydrated.

40
00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:06.146
Hydrated.

41
00:02:06.883 --> 00:02:08.128
Balanced diet.

42
00:02:09.117 --> 00:02:12.068
Balanced diet means eating the right mix of different foods.

43
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:14.787
A balanced diet keeps you strong.

44
00:02:15.383 --> 00:02:18.558
Your turn. Say: Balanced diet.

45
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.796
Balanced diet.

46
00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.470
Fatigue.

47
00:02:25.483 --> 00:02:28.121
Fatigue means a feeling of being very tired.

48
00:02:28.717 --> 00:02:30.774
Too little sleep causes fatigue.

49
00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:33.862
Your turn. Say: Fatigue.

50
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.724
Fatigue.

51
00:02:38.483 --> 00:02:39.357
Wellness.

52
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.860
Wellness means being healthy in body and mind.

53
00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.391
Our school has a wellness week.

54
00:02:45.983 --> 00:02:48.612
Your turn. Say: Wellness.

55
00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:52.630
Wellness.

56
00:02:53.383 --> 00:02:54.141
Vital.

57
00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.591
Vital means very important; necessary.

58
00:02:58.183 --> 00:03:00.253
Sleep is vital for teenagers.

59
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.479
Your turn. Say: Vital.

60
00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:07.265
Vital.

61
00:03:08.017 --> 00:03:08.925
Prevent.

62
00:03:09.917 --> 00:03:12.276
Prevent means to stop something from happening.

63
00:03:12.883 --> 00:03:14.941
Washing hands prevents illness.

64
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.028
Your turn. Say: Prevent.

65
00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:21.601
Prevent.

66
00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.318
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:27.183 --> 00:03:29.113
Visal, you look tired today.

68
00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:32.367
I have fatigue and a sore throat.

69
00:03:33.483 --> 00:03:35.936
You should drink more water and stay hydrated.

70
00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.666
Should I see a doctor?

71
00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.551
If the symptoms don't go away, you should get a checkup.

72
00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.825
Thanks. I should go to bed early to recover.

73
00:03:47.967 --> 00:03:49.630
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:50.483 --> 00:03:53.005
Grammar focus: should for health advice.

75
00:03:53.305 --> 00:03:54.492
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:55.183 --> 00:03:56.835
You should stay hydrated.

77
00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.703
You should get regular checkups.

78
00:04:00.617 --> 00:04:02.547
You should sit with good posture.

79
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.427
'should' is the same for every person: I should, he should, they should — no -s.

80
00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:11.660
Be careful! Don't say: He shoulds drink more water.

81
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.623
Say: He should drink more water.

82
00:04:15.923 --> 00:04:17.458
'Should' never takes -s.

83
00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.931
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:21.733 --> 00:04:23.466
Healthy Habits for Teens.

85
00:04:23.766 --> 00:04:26.404
Wellness means being healthy in body and mind.

86
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.050
You should stay hydrated and eat a balanced diet.

87
00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:33.834
This builds stamina and boosts your immune system.

88
00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:37.425
You should also sit with good posture when you study.

89
00:04:38.433 --> 00:04:41.722
Regular checkups are vital because they help prevent illness.

90
00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:46.812
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.243
He blank drink more water.

92
00:04:49.543 --> 00:04:53.417
A, should. B, shoulds. C, should to.

93
00:04:56.967 --> 00:04:58.606
The answer is A: should.

94
00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.761
A sign that you are ill is a blank.

95
00:05:02.061 --> 00:05:05.575
A, symptom. B, checkup. C, posture.

96
00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:11.319
The answer is A: symptom.

97
00:05:12.483 --> 00:05:14.854
To stop something from happening is to blank.

98
00:05:15.154 --> 00:05:18.460
A, prevent. B, recover. C, improve.

99
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.918
The answer is A: prevent.

100
00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:28.297
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:31.417
What do you do to stay healthy every day?

102
00:05:40.217 --> 00:05:41.926
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:42.226 --> 00:05:50.347
I drink lots of water and eat a balanced diet. I think teenagers should sleep eight hours and exercise every day.

104
00:05:50.647 --> 00:05:52.205
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:05:53.117 --> 00:05:57.394
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and should for health advice.

106
00:05:57.694 --> 00:06:02.181
Today's value is healthy living. Choose healthy food and drink lots of water.

107
00:06:02.481 --> 00:06:05.215
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:05.515 --> 00:06:08.434
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

